    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 all 28 tests pass, including both `Cp17Tests` cases (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` as a **derived-on-read** field on the Owner API, matching the existing pattern for computed fields like `membershipTier` (derived purely in the mapper, not stored on the entity).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, documenting the fixed city-to-region derivation. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `locality` accessor at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that maps the city to its canonical region:\n   - `Sydney \u2192 NSW`, `Melbourne \u2192 VIC`, `Brisbane \u2192 QLD`\n   - `UNKNOWN` for any other city\n\nI used exact-case matching to mirror the pinned reference table in the tests (`AcceptanceBase.CITY_REGION` is a case-sensitive `Map.of(...).getOrDefault(city, \"UNKNOWN\")`). Since `locality` is read-only and derived from `city`, no entity field, database column, or reverse mapping was needed.",
